# AGENTS.md — Material 3 Expressive Desktop Environment for Quickshell

> **Start here if you are writing code under `shell/`.** Run `python3 scripts/next-task.py` and do exactly what it prints, one task at a time. `python3 scripts/task-gate.py N` is the only way to finish a task: it seals the work in `docs/state/` (no git is used; never seal, revert or edit `docs/state/` yourself). Before any Quickshell/Qt API not in `docs/lld/03-guardrails.md` §5, run `python3 scripts/qs-api.py <Type> <member>`; "not found" means do not use it. If you are stuck, run `python3 scripts/task-gate.py N --stuck "<question>"` and stop. When `next-task.py` exits with 2 or 3, stop and show the human what it printed. Full rules: `docs/lld/06-unattended-runbook.md`. The end goal (a one-command install on Arch, including from a minimal install with no desktop) is in `docs/OBJECTIVE.md`; its packaging design, `docs/lld/07-distribution.md`, is not yet normative, so do not act on it during plan tasks.

> **Primary Directive for AI Coding Agents**: This repository is the authoritative Design System, Interaction Architecture, and QML Blueprint for building a complete Linux/Wayland Desktop Environment from scratch using **Quickshell** (Qt6 / QtQuick / QML) and **Material Design 3 (M3 Expressive)**.

