## 3. Mandatory Architectural Invariants (Non-Negotiable Rules)

1. **Zero Hardcoded Visual Constants**:
   - Every color MUST bind to `Tokens.color.<role>` or `Tokens.color.surfaceTier(<0..4>)`.
   - Every spacing/padding/dimension MUST bind to `Tokens.metrics.<token>`.
   - Every corner radius MUST bind to `Tokens.shape.<token>`.
   - Every animation MUST bind to `Tokens.motion.<token>`.
2. **Dual-Surface Engine Compliance (`opaque_tonal` vs. `frosted_tonal_glass`)**:
   - Root `PanelWindow` shells use **Tier 0** (`Tokens.color.surfaceTier(0)` + `Tokens.color.surfaceBorder(0)`).
   - In `frosted_tonal_glass` mode, compositor blur (`64px`) applies ONLY to the Tier 0 root container; inner interactive cards (Tier 1/2) and active accents (Tier 4) maintain `90%–100%` opacity so text legibility never drops below WCAG AA (`4.5:1`).
3. **Adaptive Desktop Paradigm Compliance (`tiling` vs. `floating`)**:
   - Every shell surface MUST react dynamically to `Tokens.desktopMode` (`"tiling"` | `"floating"`). Never require a shell restart to switch between Tiling Mode and Floating Mode.
4. **Tabular Numerals (`tnum`) on All Live Counters**:
   - Clocks, timers, battery percentages, audio percentages, CPU/RAM/network telemetry, and workspace numbers MUST set `font.features: Tokens.typography.tabularFeatures` (`{ "tnum": 1 }`) to eliminate horizontal layout jitter.
5. **M3 Expressive Spring Physics & Shape Morphing**:
   - Spatial properties (`x`, `y`, `width`, `height`, `scale`, `radius`) animate using **Spatial Springs** (`Tokens.motion.springFastSpatial`, `springDefaultSpatial`, `springSlowSpatial`), which allow subtle natural overshoot (`damping: 0.65–0.78`).
   - Visual effect properties (`color`, `opacity`, state layer alpha) animate using **Effects Curves** (`Tokens.motion.springFastEffects`, `springDefaultEffects`) with critical damping (`damping: 1.0`, zero overshoot) so colors never flash past bounds.
6. **Wayland Layer-Shell Discipline**:
   - Never use standard X11/floating `Window` for shell panels. Always use `Quickshell.Wayland.PanelWindow` with explicit `WlrLayershell.layer`, `WlrLayershell.namespace`, `WlrLayershell.exclusiveZone`, and `WlrLayershell.keyboardFocus` per `design-system/foundations/05-wayland-layershell-spatial.md`.
   - The single documented exception is the Settings app (`16-settings.md`), which is an application window (`FloatingWindow`) that users move, resize, and alt-tab to.
8. **Bars Are User Data, Never Hardcoded Layout**:
   - There is no fixed Topbar or Dock. Every bar comes from `ConfigService` `bars[]` (`01-bar-system.md`): any edge, any count, bar or island mode, start/center/end sections filled from the widget catalog (`02-bar-widgets.md`).
   - Surfaces never assume a bar edge or height: popovers use `M3Popover` origin-edge placement, and toasts, OSDs, widgets, and the Overview offset by `BarService.insets(screen)` with `ExclusionMode.Ignore`.
   - Respect the bar guardrails: security indicators always have a home (fallback pill), core actions stay keybound, and bars stay within the thickness and space bounds.
7. **Usability & Accessibility Contract (Flair Never Costs Function)** — `design-system/foundations/04-interaction-states-and-input.md`:
   - Honor `Tokens.reducedMotion`, `expressiveSprings`, `reducedTransparency`, `highContrast`, and `textScale` live: gate spatial Behaviors with `Tokens.motion.spatialMotionEnabled` and decorative loops with `decorativeMotionEnabled`; never hardcode type sizes.
   - Every interactive element is keyboard-reachable (`activeFocusOnTab`, `Enter`/`Space`, `Menu`/`Shift+F10`), shows the focus ring only under `Tokens.keyboardModality`, and sets `Accessible.name` (mandatory for icon-only controls, together with an `M3Tooltip`).
   - Middle-click, right-click, and scroll are accelerators only: never destructive, never the only path; wheel input accumulates (`wheelStepAngle`, `touchpadStepPixels`).
   - Bar targets meet `Tokens.metrics.minPointerTarget`, extend through screen margins to the physical edge, and never change width on hover.
   - Expressive polygons, editorial serif, and duotone numerals stay within their placement guardrails (`03-motion-and-morphing.md` §5, `02-typography-and-iconography.md` §4); text on the wallpaper follows the Legibility Guard (`01-color-and-surfaces.md` §5).

