## 4. Recommended 9-Phase Implementation Order for AI Agents

When asked to build the full Quickshell Desktop Environment from this design system, follow the task plan in `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-27-mat-shell-implementation-plan.md`. It refines the 9 phases below into 34 tasks and moves pure logic and core services ahead of primitives, because primitives depend on `ShellState`, `BarService` and `KeyboardService`. Paths in `docs/lld/01-architecture.md` (`shell/MatShell/Tokens/`, `shell/MatShell/Services/`) supersede the `shell/tokens/` / `shell/services/` mentions here (LLD C20). The phases, for orientation:

1. **Phase 1 — Token Singletons & Theme Pipeline**: Copy `design-system/tokens/qml/` into `shell/tokens/` (`ColorTokens` already watches `~/.config/mat-shell/theme.json`) and `design-system/tokens/matugen/` into `~/.config/mat-shell/matugen/`. Verify with `matugen color hex "#6750A4" -c ~/.config/mat-shell/matugen/config.toml` (output must equal `theme.baseline.json`), then a wallpaper run with `--source-color-index 0`, and confirm live hot-reload plus instant Dark/Light switching.
2. **Phase 2 — Core Primitives**: Implement `M3Surface`, `M3StateLayer`, `M3Button`, `M3IconButton`, `M3BarPill`, `M3Switch`, `M3Slider`, `M3TextField`, `M3Popover`, `M3Tooltip`, `M3ContextMenu`, `M3PolygonSurface`, `M3AppIcon`, `M3DuotoneClock`, and `M3HoldToConfirm` — each with the keyboard and `Accessible` contract built in.
3. **Phase 3 — Global `ShellState`, Services & Wayland Screen Corners**: Create the root `ShellState.qml` singleton (mutual exclusion lanes, security-modal protection, multi-instance trigger registry with origin edge, Bar Focus Mode, IPC incl. `openSettings`), the service singletons from `03-quickshell-service-architecture.md` (including `ConfigService`, `BarService`, `BarWidgetRegistry`, `KeybindService`, `AccessibilityService`, and `KeyboardService`), and per-monitor `M3ScreenCorners`.
4. **Phase 4 — Bar System, Bar Widgets & OSD HUDs**: Implement `01-bar-system.md` (config-driven bars on any edge, bar/island mode, sections, visibility, guardrails) and `02-bar-widgets.md` (widget registry with horizontal/vertical variants, including `apps` for docks and taskbars), shipping the "Top bar + Dock" preset as the default, then `07-osd-huds.md`.
5. **Phase 5 — Popover Triad (Control Center, Calendar/Weather, Media)**: Implement `03-control-center.md`, `05-calendar-and-weather.md`, and `06-media-player-popover.md` on `M3Popover`, with shared-origin morphing from bar widgets on any edge.
6. **Phase 6 — Notification Server (Toasts & Notification Center)**: Implement `04-notifications.md` bound to `Quickshell.Services.Notifications`.
7. **Phase 7 — Settings App**: Implement `16-settings.md` (two-pane window, Bars editor with live preview and sections editor, Keybindings, Animations, Accessibility, About), verifying every preset in `m3-tokens.json` `modes.bars.presets` renders correctly on all four edges.
8. **Phase 8 — Full-Screen Overlays & Desktop Widgets (Launcher, Overview, Capture, Theme Studio, Widgets Layer)**: Implement `08-app-and-command-launcher.md`, `09-workspace-and-window-overview.md`, `13-screen-capture-and-recording.md`, `14-wallpaper-and-theme-picker.md`, and `15-desktop-widgets-layer.md` (requires `M3PolygonSurface`, `M3AppIcon`, and `M3DuotoneClock` from Phase 2).
9. **Phase 9 — Security & Session Surfaces (Lock Screen, Power Menu, Polkit)**: Implement `10-lock-screen.md` (`WlSessionLock`), `11-power-and-session-menu.md`, and `12-polkit-authentication-dialog.md`.
